Bridge 0134 (G7): a converted YCbCr texture's linear sample is the device's bilinear filter. CoreAnimation's composite sampled the
YCBCR8_420_2P slot (0131's converted RGBA16F image) through the exact routine on Turnip: 4 RGBA16F taps plus Metal's integer sums
(grid 2048, each 2D term truncated by 2^7) per fragment, because the format's TexelFormat class carries EXACT and only a MetalSampler
device (MoltenVK) leaves it to the device. Now the binder's TexelFormat(slot) specialization drops EXACT for a PackedTexels::YCbCr2048
format (the 8- and 10-bit converted two-plane formats, packed or not, every subsampling) on a device without Metal's own sampler: the
linear sample takes the module's existing device arm (lower::sampler::linear device_when, class without a measured family). The packed
field stays, so reads, nearest samples and gathers convert as before (half.rs/float_texel.rs ignore EXACT for a packed class). The
slot's VkSampler is the Metal sampler's (LINEAR), checked against the view format at bind (check_filter_features); Turnip gives
R16G16B16A16_SFLOAT SAMPLED_IMAGE_FILTER_LINEAR (tu_formats.cc tu_format_linear_filtering_supported: only a702 refuses some formats).
Cache: the SPIR-V and the disk artifacts are unchanged (the class is a specialization value set per draw, slots.rs bound_value); the
pipeline variant key and the driver's VkPipelineCache record name the specialization, so the exact-routine variant is a separate entry.
Error vs the exact routine (model, 8-bit subtexel weights): at most 8/2048 per colour channel rounding the weights (16/2048 truncating)
at a 0 <-> 1 edge, under 1.7/2048 on smooth content; alpha exact. The pipeline announces ycbcr-filter-not-exact. Not covered: heap
(argument buffer) textures, extended-range (XR) and sRGB/12-bit formats (other fields), keep the exact routine. Reuse: none upstream
(upstream metal2vulkan emulates the filter on every non-Metal device).
Off: SWEET_YCBCR_HWFILTER=0. Logs "SWEET_YCBCR_HWFILTER mode N" once (with SWEET_PIPESTATS).

